tleE2eTest` opens `/products/no-such-product` and asserts \"404\", \"Page Not Found\" and the full message text.\n- **The shop title:** the same browser test asserts the tab title \"domaincentric.commerce\".\n- **The two links:** two integration tests in `NotFoundPageTest` open the not-found page, check the 404 status and the link label, follow the link and assert the heading of the page it leads to. The recorded break patches turn each of them red.\n- **Test runs:** the story's test-stage gate reports all mapped tests green. The browser test was also green after it gained its extra assertions, in the `not-found-title` build gate at 13:13.\n\nThere is one minor finding, and it does not block. At `NotFoundTitleE2eTest.cs:21`, the heading \"Page Not Found\" is checked as text anywhere on the page, not as a heading element. The fix is to read the heading element itself, `h2.error-page__title`.\n\nCAT-03 depends on `not-found-title`, and that change is still uncommitted in the working tree. So the title scenario only holds once that story is committed. I changed no code and ran no other stage.","ttft_ms":3323,"type":"result","duration_ms":55269,"uuid":"526eb4ad-743b-4053-830c-4f826c96cf93","ttft_stream_ms":2443,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":2443,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
